  "title": "`getCirculatingSupplyAndAssets` Relies on Unstable `rBalance`, Leading to Incorrect Share Conversions",
  "body": "## Summary\n\nThe function `getCirculatingSupplyAndAssets` is used during share-to-asset and asset-to-share conversions. It relies on `totalInvestmentAssets`, which includes `rBalance` from the investment share token. However, `rBalance` is not stable and can be reversed via `WERC7575ShareToken::cancelrBalanceAdjustment`. If `rBalance` is later corrected, users whose deposits or redemptions were executed based on the incorrect value will receive inaccurate share amounts or asset amounts, effectively causing value shifts between users.\n\n## Root Cause\n\n`_calculateInvestmentAssets` adds both the investment share token balance and its `rBalance`:\n\n```solidity\n// Add invested assets from the investment ShareToken (if configured)\ntotalNormalizedAssets += _calculateInvestmentAssets();\n\n// _calculateInvestmentAssets\nfunction _calculateInvestmentAssets() internal view returns (uint256 totalInvestmentAssets) {\n    ShareTokenStorage storage $ = _getShareTokenStorage();\n    address investmentShareToken = $.investmentShareToken;\n\n    if (investmentShareToken == address(0)) {\n        return 0;\n    }\n\n    // Balance of investment ShareToken (normalized to 18 decimals)\n    totalInvestmentAssets = IERC20(investmentShareToken).balanceOf(address(this));\n\n    // Add rBalance if supported\n    try IWERC7575ShareToken(investmentShareToken).rBalanceOf(address(this)) returns (uint256 rShares) {\n        totalInvestmentAssets += rShares;\n    } catch {\n        // Ignore if rBalanceOf is not supported\n    }\n}\n```\n\nHowever, `rBalance` is not immutable. It can be reverted through `cancelrBalanceAdjustment`:\n\n```solidity\nfunction cancelrBalanceAdjustment(address account, uint256 ts) external onlyRevenueAdmin {\n    if (_rBalanceAdjustments[account][ts][0] == 0) {\n        revert NoRBalanceAdjustmentFound();\n    }\n\n    uint256[2] memory adjustment = _rBalanceAdjustments[account][ts];\n    uint256 amounti = adjustment[0];\n    uint256 amountr = adjustment[1];\n\n    if (amountr > amounti) {\n        uint256 difference = amountr - amounti;\n        uint256 currentRBalance = _rBalances[account];\n        if (currentRBalance < difference) {\n            revert RBalanceAdjustmentTooLarge();\n        } else {\n            unchecked {\n                _rBalances[account] -= difference;\n            }\n        }\n    } else if (amountr < amounti) {\n        uint256 difference = amounti - amountr;\n        unchecked {\n            _rBalances[account] += difference;\n        }\n    }\n\n    delete _rBalanceAdjustments[account][ts];\n    emit RBalanceAdjustmentCancelled(account, ts);\n}\n```\n\nBecause deposits and redemptions use this value at execution time, any later correction to `rBalance` introduces inconsistency and unintended wealth transfer between users.\n\n## Mitigation\n\nDo not include `rBalance` in investment asset calculations, as these balances are not realized. Only add them once they are fully realized and reflected in the actual vault asset balance. This prevents reversible or incorrect `rBalance` adjustments from corrupting share conversion logic.\n\n---",
